 "veredito_vs_criterio": "with the 200-seed reference (g10b2, 16 cells): the exact expectation STILL does NOT reduce the error against the nodal retention in ANY of the comparisons -- same direction as the earlier outcome (mean field > nodal, exact even further below, correction in the wrong direction). Changing the reference from 20 to 200 seeds SHRANK the absolute error of both (nodal fell ~3%, moving closer to the mean field) but did NOT change the sign of the comparison: the mean field remains closer to nodal than the exact expectation in all g10b2 cells tested. Outcome kept: Table 2 keeps the mean field as the central number; the exact expectation gains no support with the corrected reference.",
 "nao_verificado": [
  {
   "item": "correlation between test blocks (pairs/triplets) beyond the mean effect of sampling without replacement",
   "motivo": "lattice_retention() models the probability of EACH individual trimming neighbour being a test block via the marginal hypergeometric (falling factorial), not the exact joint distribution of the 8 neighbours of a block under the simultaneous draw of the n_g groups -- a reasonable approximation for the n_te,N involved (n_te/N ~0.15-0.17), but it is not the full multivariate hypergeometric; not quantified in this round due to budget."
  }
 ],
